creen  time Google's well-being controls for  the newest version of Android which  pretty much no one has yet automatically  switches to grayscale at the end of the  day yes so Apple buries the grayscale  setting deep in here you have to go to  Settings General accessibility display  accommodations flick on color filters  and then grayscale on Wednesday morning  I was playing with my son before  breakfast but then I wanted to take a  photo of him naturally being the cutest  kid in the world and it was hard to tell  what I was actually capturing through  the black-and-white viewfinder but  there's actually a good trick back in  those accessibility settings if you can  find those again you can program the  button on the side of the iPhone to  launch color filters Wow  it's it's beautiful the blue and the  Twitter it's like I smoked a Crayola  crayon so I've decided I'm going to go  gray when I really want to enforce my  limits and I think that's gonna be a  good chunk of my day it's just been way  more effective for me than Apple's easy  to override screen time limits it's like  trying to put a lock on a cigarette pack  but for now this is helping me look up  from my phone and discover all the color  in my real world  [Music]

